---
import Page from "../../src/layouts/Page.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../src/config";
import { TOTALS } from "../../src/lib/national";
---
<Page title="How it works" seoTitle={`How ${SITE.brand} Works: Our Referral Model, Explained`} description={`${SITE.brand} is an independent referral service. Here's how calls are routed, who pays us, and what that means for you.`} eyebrow="About" path="/how-it-works/">
  <p class="lede">{SITE.brand} is a referral service. We publish free county guides for homeowners in {TOTALS.states} states and connect callers with restoration companies that serve their area. We don't do restoration work ourselves.</p>

  <h2>What happens when you call</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><strong>Your call is routed by location.</strong> The number on each county page connects to a participating restoration company that serves that county. You may hear a short automated prompt that confirms your location and the type of damage.</li>
    <li><strong>A local company answers.</strong> You talk directly with the company that would do the work. They'll ask what happened and arrange an inspection.</li>
    <li><strong>You decide.</strong> You're never obligated to hire the company you're connected with. Get a written estimate, ask questions, and compare if you want to.</li>
  </ol>
  {SITE.launchMode !== "live" && <p class="notice notice-amber">The call line isn't live yet. Until it is, the call buttons on this site lead to this page.</p>}

  <h2>How we're paid</h2>
  <p>Restoration companies, or the call networks that work with them, pay us when we refer a caller. There's no charge to you for the referral. The company you hire bills you or your insurer for its work, the same as if you'd found it yourself.</p>

  <h2>What payment doesn't change</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Our guides are written to help you limit damage and protect your claim, including steps that mean you may need less professional work.</li>
    <li>We don't rank, review or endorse individual companies, and we don't publish testimonials.</li>
    <li>We're not affiliated with any insurance company or government agency.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We don't inspect, quote, or perform any work.</li>
    <li>We don't guarantee response times, prices or workmanship. Those are between you and the company.</li>
    <li>We don't sell your information. See our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Before you hire anyone</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Ask whether technicians are IICRC certified.</li>
    <li>Ask for proof of insurance and any local registration or license your city or county requires.</li>
    <li>Get the scope and price in writing, and read anything you sign.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Questions or concerns: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a></p>
</Page>
